[18:35:25] I've redrawn the beetle as a Solo48 model and `validate_icon()` returns `valid` with no warnings. I fixed every issue in the metrics list except one. When I ran `svg_metrics.py` on the redraw as a cross-check, it still reported the head and shell as 0 apart, which I couldn't fix (explained below).

**Drawing:** a side view of a bug facing right. The spiral shell is one continuous line: it forms the dome, then curls under the body and turns in to a small inner curl. A round head touches the front of the shell, two antennae fan out from the side of the head away from the shell, and two legs each have a shin and a forward-pointing foot, as in the image. I took the spiral built from nested arcs and the head touching the shell from Lucide's `snail`, but spaced the turns 9 apart.

**Keyshape:** `HRECT_L`, not the suggested `SQUARE`. At stroke 4 the drawing needs 40 units of width (shell 26, head 10, plus the antennae), and `SQUARE` only allows 36. The metrics also rate `HRECT_L` as the closer fit. The drawing reaches all four sides of the box exactly.

**Dropped from the image:** the closed outer circle of the shell and its 1.5-turn inner spiral. At stroke 4, that many turns can't keep 8 units apart inside the shell, so the outer shell line itself becomes the spiral.

**Metric issues:**

| Issue | Result |
|---|---|
| Stroke width 2.4 in the trace (info) | Drawn at 4, with all gaps sized for it |
| 12 strokes, budget 6 | Fixed: now 6 (shell, head, two antennae, two legs) |
| Keyshape only 86% tall | Fixed: `HRECT_L`, all four sides reached exactly |
| Spiral too close to the shell wall, head and legs (1.5–7.9 apart) | Fixed: spiral and shell are one line, turns 9 apart, inner curl 9 from the head |
| Antennae 2.6 apart and 6.5 from the shell | Fixed: they share one root on the head and stay at least 8.4 apart (9.5 at the tips) and 8.2 from the shell |
| Leg pieces and shell bottom 2.6–7.8 apart | Fixed: each leg is one stroke, legs at least 8.8 apart |
| Holes 4.56 / 1.34 / 3.16 wide (need 6) | Fixed: the head's hole measures 5.88 on the raster and passes the metrics check; no other closed holes remain |
| **Head and shell 0 apart (new, from the cross-check)** | **Not fixable in the drawing.** The head is meant to touch the shell at (30,21), the contact is declared, and the validator accepts it. The script only recognises contact at the ends of lines, and here the head meets the middle of the shell's line. |

**Visual check:** at 48 px on light and dark backgrounds the spiral, head, antennae and legs all read clearly. The short tail at the back of the shell is the spiral's outer end.

The module isn't registered under `icon_set/model/icons`, `published/` is untouched, and I didn't run the build or gallery updates.

